    "description": "Electronic harassment, electromagnetic torture, and psychotronic torture is a conspiracy theory describing the hostile use of mundane electromagnetic devices, such as radio or microwaves, against...",
    "content": "Electronic harassment, electromagnetic torture, and psychotronic torture is a conspiracy theory describing the hostile use of mundane electromagnetic devices, such as radio or microwaves, against self-identified \"targeted individuals\" (TIs). They believe that malicious actors are transmitting sounds and thoughts into people's heads, affecting their bodies, and harassing them generally. The delusion often concerns government agents or crime rings and alleges that the \"perpetrators\" use electromagnetic radiation (such as the microwave auditory effect), radar, and surveillance techniques to carry out their goals. \nSome TIs claim to be victims of gang stalking, and many have created or joined support and advocacy groups.\nMultiple medical professionals have concluded that these experiences are hallucinations, the result of delusional disorders, or psychosis.",
